From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: relax nommu access_ok

The generic NOMMU mmap path returns directly allocated kernel addresses. MIPS
access_ok still applies the MMU user segment limit, causing binfmt_flat
read_code() to fail with -EFAULT before first userspace. Trust NOMMU addresses
for this bring-up so FLAT init can be loaded and executed.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/uaccess.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/uaccess.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/uaccess.h
index 3975394..449beba 100644
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/uaccess.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/uaccess.h
@@ -126,7 +126,11 @@ static inline int __access_ok(const void __user *p, unsigned long size)
 static inline int __access_ok(const void __user *p, unsigned long size)
 {
+#ifndef CONFIG_MMU
+	return 1;
+#else
 	unsigned long addr = (unsigned long)p;
 	return (get_fs().seg & (addr | (addr + size) | __ua_size(size))) == 0;
+#endif
 }
 
 #define access_ok(addr, size)					\
-- 
